---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Crown FM"
  description="Crown FM is a facilities management business serving commercial property owners and occupiers — directly-employed engineers, transparent contracts, one point of contact."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:py-20">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-wide uppercase text-brand-700">
      About Crown FM
    </p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-brand-900 max-w-3xl">
      Facilities management without the games.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg text-slate-600">
      We're a directly-employed FM team for commercial property — offices,
      light industrial, retail estates and multi-let buildings. We don't
      sub-contract the work we sold you, and we don't pad the invoice when
      something breaks.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-slate-200 bg-brand-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-900">Why we started</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          Most facilities contracts are designed around the supplier's
          margin, not the building. You get tiered help desks, sub-contractors
          two layers deep, and compliance certificates that don't quite line
          up with the assets in your basement.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          Crown FM exists because we think the job is more straightforward
          than that. Know the assets. Service them on time. Pick up the phone
          when something breaks. Keep the paperwork tidy. Charge fairly.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-900">How we work</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-slate-600">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-brand-900">One point of contact.</strong>
            A named account manager who knows your building and answers their
            phone. Not a ticket queue.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-brand-900">Directly-employed engineers.</strong>
            Our engineers are on our payroll, in our vans, in our uniform.
            The people on site are the people we trained.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-brand-900">Transparent commercials.</strong>
            Fixed PPM fee, published rate card for reactive works, supplier
            invoices passed through at cost.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-brand-900">Audit-ready records.</strong>
            Every visit, certificate and asset history in one place, available
            to you on demand.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-slate-200">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-900">Who we work with</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        We're a good fit if you're responsible for keeping one or more
        commercial buildings running — and the current arrangement is
        eating more of your week than it should.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-10 grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6">
        <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-brand-900">Office occupiers</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
            Single-site HQs and multi-floor tenants who need the building to
            be invisible.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-brand-900">Landlords &amp; managing agents</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
            Common parts, plant rooms and statutory compliance across a
            portfolio.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-brand-900">Light industrial</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
            Warehouses, depots and workshops where downtime has a daily cost.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="border border-slate-200 rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-brand-900">Retail &amp; hospitality</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
            Trading hours that don't bend, and a maintenance window that's
            always last night.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-slate-200 bg-brand-900">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 flex flex-col md:flex-row justify-between items-start md:items-center gap-6">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-white">
          Want to see what we'd do differently?
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-brand-100 max-w-xl">
          Send us your current schedule of works and we'll mark it up
          honestly. No pitch deck.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a
        href="/contact"
        class="inline-flex items-center rounded-md bg-white px-5 py-3 text-brand-900 font-medium hover:bg-brand-50 transition"
        >Get in touch</a
      >
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
